  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "Consider the Fibonacci sequence, given by $F_{k+1}=F_k+F_{k-1}$ for $k\\ge2$, where the first two terms are $F_1=1$ and $F_2=1$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p33-q11-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Prove that\n$$F_{k+1}^{2}-F_k^{2}=F_{k-1}F_{k+2}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$F_{k+1}^{2}-F_k^{2}=(F_{k+1}-F_k)(F_{k+1}+F_k)=F_{k-1}F_{k+2}$.",
          "worked": "Using the Fibonacci recurrence,\n$$\\begin{align*}F_{k+1}^{2}-F_k^{2}&=(F_{k+1}-F_k)(F_{k+1}+F_k)\\\\F_{k+1}^{2}-F_k^{2}&=F_{k-1}F_{k+2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q11-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, simplify\n$$F_1F_4+F_2F_5+\\cdots+F_{n-1}F_{n+2}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$F_{n+1}^{2}-1$.\n\nUse part (a) to write each product as a difference of consecutive squares; the intermediate terms cancel.",
          "worked": "Apply part (a) for $k=2,3,\\ldots,n$:\n$$\\begin{align*}F_1F_4+F_2F_5+\\cdots+F_{n-1}F_{n+2}&=(F_3^2-F_2^2)+(F_4^2-F_3^2)+\\cdots+(F_{n+1}^2-F_n^2)\\\\F_1F_4+F_2F_5+\\cdots+F_{n-1}F_{n+2}&=F_{n+1}^2-F_2^2\\\\F_1F_4+F_2F_5+\\cdots+F_{n-1}F_{n+2}&=F_{n+1}^2-1.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 39
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q11-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Prove that\n$$\\frac1{F_k}-\\frac1{F_{k+1}}=\\frac{F_{k-1}}{F_kF_{k+1}}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac1{F_k}-\\dfrac1{F_{k+1}}=\\dfrac{F_{k+1}-F_k}{F_kF_{k+1}}=\\dfrac{F_{k-1}}{F_kF_{k+1}}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1{F_k}-\\frac1{F_{k+1}}&=\\frac{F_{k+1}-F_k}{F_kF_{k+1}}\\\\\\frac1{F_k}-\\frac1{F_{k+1}}&=\\frac{F_{k-1}}{F_kF_{k+1}}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q11-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Hence, simplify\n$$\\frac{F_1}{F_2F_3}+\\frac{F_2}{F_3F_4}+\\cdots+\\frac{F_{n-1}}{F_nF_{n+1}}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1-\\dfrac1{F_{n+1}}$.\n\nUse part (c) to write each term as a difference of reciprocals; the intermediate terms cancel.",
          "worked": "Apply part (c) for $k=2,3,\\ldots,n$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{F_1}{F_2F_3}+\\frac{F_2}{F_3F_4}+\\cdots+\\frac{F_{n-1}}{F_nF_{n+1}}&=\\left(\\frac1{F_2}-\\frac1{F_3}\\right)+\\left(\\frac1{F_3}-\\frac1{F_4}\\right)+\\cdots+\\left(\\frac1{F_n}-\\frac1{F_{n+1}}\\right)\\\\\\frac{F_1}{F_2F_3}+\\frac{F_2}{F_3F_4}+\\cdots+\\frac{F_{n-1}}{F_nF_{n+1}}&=\\frac1{F_2}-\\frac1{F_{n+1}}\\\\\\frac{F_1}{F_2F_3}+\\frac{F_2}{F_3F_4}+\\cdots+\\frac{F_{n-1}}{F_nF_{n+1}}&=1-\\frac1{F_{n+1}}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      }
    ]
  },
